[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   step_121: Masked-signal discrimination on the post-2017 cohort.
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   Steps 117-120 established the prospective failure and its anatomy: the
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   post-2017 SBDB cohort does not replicate the declared-axis anomaly and
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   carries instead a cohort-private, unipolar dipole at (120,-40) whose
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   amplitude (0.48 dex maximum cap-gap) is comparable to the anomaly
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   itself.  Section 4.12 registers the remaining discrimination: is the
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   declared-axis signal ABSENT in this cohort, or PRESENT BUT MASKED by
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   the additive private structure?  A private dipole of that size,
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   displaced ~79 deg from the declared axis, mechanically depresses the
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   in-cap contrast whether or not a boundary signal sits underneath.
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   This step resolves the discrimination by joint two-component
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   decomposition.  The residual field of every cohort is modelled as
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   y_i = a + A * s_i(declared cap) + B * cos(theta_i -> u_priv) + e_i
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   where s_i is the 60-deg cap indicator about the declared transit axis
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   (34,-13) -- the template the CODE rotation anomaly follows (one-ended,
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   threshold at 60-75 deg) -- and cos(theta -> u_priv) is the unipolar
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   basis step_118 established for the private structure (cos1 dominant,
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   cos2 null).  The masked-signal hypothesis predicts A > 0 once B is
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   fitted; the absent-signal hypothesis predicts A ~ 0 at every dipole
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   placement.
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   Tests
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   T1  joint fit on the prospective cohort: declared-cap coefficient A
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   before vs after absorbing the private dipole; bootstrap CI and
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   label-permutation null on A_joint; masking budget
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   B * (median cos_priv in-cap - out-cap).
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   T2  dipole-direction robustness scan: the joint fit repeated at
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   every grid axis u_priv -- the range of A over all dipole
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   placements, the best-fit dipole, and whether ANY placement
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   simultaneously fits the private structure and drives A <= 0.
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   Nested-model evidence: delta-RSS of the joint model over the
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   dipole-only model, permutation-tested.
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   T3  clean-stratum declared-axis tests: the strata step_119 found
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   dipole-free (hyperbolic e >= 1; one-sided arcs) are scored at
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   the declared axis directly -- if the anomaly is object-
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   associated, the least-masked members should carry it.
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   T4  identical joint fit on the two control cohorts: CODE (A > 0,
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   B ~ 0 expected) and pre-2018 SBDB (both ~ 0 expected).
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   T5  cohort x cap interaction after dipole correction: the step_118
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   interaction (p = 0.005) re-measured on the dipole-subtracted
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   prospective field -- how much of the CODE-vs-prospective
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   inconsistency the masking accounts for.
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   T6  declared-axis profile before vs after dipole subtraction:
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   cap gap, Spearman vs theta, and the declared axis's rank in the
[2026-09-20 12:22:20 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 121]   free scan of the corrected field.
